{"allowed_english": [], "context": {"approved_glossary_entries": [], "input_freeze": {"hash": "sha256:bcbed34fc6e099ef2da4c4e37ca5b026a4235b89e8d2ec786595f6e753742671", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p011-frozen.json"}, "locked_english_contexts": {"inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0005": {"context_hash": "sha256:303ba97d456a78831dc8b6efc42a5f8eec30a6dab5a234efd43596939fa193f0", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0005", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 252880, "byte_start": 252187, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:42197066673b5695fd5176785c113fbd5ed893a188d036cad08ca75d92451710", "line_end": 7165, "line_start": 7155}, "owner_tag": "003S", "parent_tag": "003S", "semantic_path": "paragraph/0005", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0003": "$U \\in \\Ob(\\mathcal{C})$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0009": "$G \\to H$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-group-homomorphism-fibreedingroupoids}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4e642e75a93b521151d71c3ddd3db4c5c27f97f30718fd2700af944e920de03a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1fefe2401536d2a1b575e4087afc5605fbc801a915f003cf99840e93ff4c0c92", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nGiven <MATH_0001>, we can ask: if the fibre\ncategory <MATH_0002> is a groupoid for all <MATH_0003>,\nmust <MATH_0004> be fibred in groupoids over <MATH_0005>? We can see the\nanswer is no as follows. Start with a category fibred in groupoids\n<MATH_0006>. Altering the morphisms in <MATH_0007>\nwhich do not map to the identity morphism on some object does not alter the\ncategories <MATH_0008>. Hence we can violate the existence and uniqueness\nconditions on lifts. One example is the functor from Example\n<REF_0001> when <MATH_0009> is not\nsurjective. Here is another example.", "source_text_hash": "sha256:ec0d570058aac129b5e3a4b031c0ce9c3e8549b75f039e21cade5246bdb57a7e", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:003S:paragraph/0005"}, "state": "READY"}, "inventory:categories:03WQ:proof/0001": {"context_hash": "sha256:6a7fd6ca4770ab9531640a75f6a03b888c323a3a4b51e012ca207f1c35d0e585", "inventory_id": "inventory:categories:03WQ:proof/0001", "kind": "locked-English-neighbor", "location": {"byte_end": 251671, "byte_start": 250312, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:4d557776532800b848fca8fb0fd993f580302ead27a30f8d38a2a091e15dc573", "line_end": 7142, "line_start": 7117}, "owner_tag": "03WQ", "parent_tag": "003S", "semantic_path": "proof/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0002": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$x$", "MATH_0004": "$U$", "MATH_0005": "$\\varphi : y \\to x$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$p' : \\mathcal{S}' \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0009": "$\\phi$", "MATH_0010": "$\\psi$", "MATH_0011": "$\\gamma$", "MATH_0012": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0013": "$\\gamma$", "MATH_0014": "$\\phi \\circ \\psi$", "MATH_0015": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0016": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0017": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "MATH_0018": "$\\mathcal{S}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-composition-cartesian}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{definition-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{definition-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0004": "\\ref{definition-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0005": "\\ref{equation-fibred-groupoids}", "REF_0006": "\\ref{definition-cartesian-over-C}", "REF_0007": "\\ref{lemma-composition-cartesian}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{proof}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{proof}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9b4b50669512c2a3a84986ad0c6db8ae41541ee1c803cfe16fcdacaed2d1e871", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:897db494ee51f7eb24f245c1d4ab1a1a251d82c516755e1b935834b1ff00933d", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that the construction makes sense since by\nLemma <REF_0001>\nthe identity morphism of any object of <MATH_0001> is strongly cartesian,\nand the composition of strongly cartesian morphisms is strongly cartesian.\nThe first lifting property of\nDefinition <REF_0002>\nfollows from the condition that in a fibred category\ngiven any morphism <MATH_0002> and <MATH_0003> lying over <MATH_0004> there exists\na strongly cartesian morphism <MATH_0005> lying over <MATH_0006>.\nLet us check the second lifting property of\nDefinition <REF_0003>\nfor the category <MATH_0007> over <MATH_0008>.\nTo do this we argue as in the discussion following\nDefinition <REF_0004>.\nThus in Diagram <REF_0005> the\nmorphisms <MATH_0009>, <MATH_0010> and <MATH_0011> are strongly cartesian morphisms\nof <MATH_0012>.\nHence <MATH_0013> and <MATH_0014> are strongly cartesian morphisms\nof <MATH_0015> lying over the same arrow of <MATH_0016> and\nhaving the same target in <MATH_0017>. By the discussion following\nDefinition <REF_0006>\nthis means these two arrows are isomorphic as desired (here we use also\nthat any isomorphism in <MATH_0018> is strongly cartesian, by\nLemma <REF_0007> again).\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:b4c49660568ae62b7d33697d42d967301fcba30d79977e7846fff1a566b20f7a", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:03WQ:proof/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "reference:categories-example-group-groupoid": {"context_hash": "sha256:c944df3d591a28db3a0274238a3bbf11c35341d4f5539d08f6a4ab9874c12fe7", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 5820, "byte_start": 5556, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:50d7f6d49667f153c2560dbdb569f431ad8895ec83f586c4fc67649cd6401b9d", "line_end": 152, "line_start": 146}, "owner_tag": "0019", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-example-group-groupoid", "requested_tag": "0019", "semantic_path": "example/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{example-group-groupoid}", "MATH_0001": "$G$", "MATH_0002": "$x$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Mor(x, x) = G$", "MATH_0004": "$G$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{example}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{example}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:383823b46a4447bf4e5335d11566309cb0b9ddcc760a75daa49f005fc3a29836", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:5d7defcfde475969ada7e7fead563e2f313b7a87bd5ad38f3ed828441792a7e9", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nA group <MATH_0001> gives rise to a groupoid with a single object <MATH_0002>\nand morphisms <MATH_0003>, with the composition rule\ngiven by the group law in <MATH_0004>. Every groupoid with a single\nobject is of this form.\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:004305b936af192dfb112f544eb8d16a3d3857340d59767ebad354a642ee77a5", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0019:example/0001"}, "state": "READY"}, "reference:categories-example-group-homomorphism-functor": {"context_hash": "sha256:67f06242e0f87a57c6e03a6cc309eaff8fe481a10be9a21c9321245b2ccdb2ac", "kind": "locked-English-reference", "location": {"byte_end": 9793, "byte_start": 9489, "file": "categories.tex", "fragment_hash": "sha256:f98ac2339eb11545b4ca80fdc8fdab070705b99681d5741845f57f005d95834a", "line_end": 252, "line_start": 246}, "owner_tag": "001F", "parent_tag": "0013", "requested_label": "categories-example-group-homomorphism-functor", "requested_tag": "001F", "semantic_path": "example/0001", "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_unit": {"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "0013", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\label{example-group-homomorphism-functor}", "MATH_0001": "$p : G\\to H$", "MATH_0002": "$p$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-group-groupoid}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{example}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\end{example}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:907dd579c3eb4d4adf277167e56cda44dad8836e0a96f81e61866246f022dcd0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:b172ff296f04008f0832d4aca045cbd91d5128646499737c4fd1c70b193d5983", "source_text": "<STRUCT_0001>\n<LOCKED_0001>\nA homomorphism <MATH_0001> of groups gives rise to a functor\nbetween the associated groupoids in Example <REF_0001>. It is\nfaithful (resp.<SPACE_0001>fully faithful) if and only if <MATH_0002> is injective (resp.<SPACE_0002>an\nisomorphism).\n<STRUCT_0002>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:a804b03077090d44b6dc075c1afba01554741b21fc18e7b68447dc6d038b76f5", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:001F:example/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:c34bcf1feb77b9a354318826bc79563eec8647bae36c4c37e1d8bccf6154513b", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p011-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:6d1de43433dd40188a7252ad9518957470cf80b4ad4aaf92f76c3110206a9c94"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": [], "policy_revision": "git:b33b9b37f1623d49d4030a11f1661dfc29fa2ce4", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:03WQ:proof/0001", "relation": "before"},